Against inter-sensor distance, the modeled magnetometer correlations followed the measured ones at << F.wr_cov_dist_d25_50_label >>~mm (<< F.rev_cov_dist_mag_d25_50_model_r >> against << F.rev_cov_dist_mag_d25_50_measured_r >>) and fell faster beyond, to << F.rev_cov_dist_mag_d200_225_model_r >> against << F.rev_cov_dist_mag_d200_225_measured_r >> at << F.wr_cov_dist_d200_225_label >>~mm (Fig.~\ref{fig:S3}D). Spatially correlated backgrounds did not change this, because the measured long-range correlation is a far-field pattern, not a cortical one. The gradiometers' median signed correlations agreed at every distance (<< F.rev_cov_dist_grad_d25_50_model_r >> against << F.rev_cov_dist_grad_d25_50_measured_r >> at << F.wr_cov_dist_d25_50_label >>~mm; Fig.~\ref{fig:S3}E).

