\subsection{Sensitivity analyses}\label{sec:S3.6}

Each analysis changed one element of the adult model (the joint runs, several) and recalibrated the background; intervals are from << F.meth_boot_noise_sens >> parcel-bootstrap resamples of one anatomy. The spike simulations were not repeated under these alternatives.

The primary model omits the cortex within << F.rev_ns_near_rule_mm >>~mm of the inner skull: << F.rev_ns_near_n_vertices >> white-surface vertices (<< F.rev_ns_near_share_valid_pct >> of the valid ones) and << F.rev_ns_near_area_cm2 >>~cm² of cortex (<< F.rev_ns_near_area_pct >>). Because lead fields are not converged closer than about << F.rev_ns_joint_floor_mm >>~mm to the inner-skull mesh, the primary variants add the cortex from << F.rev_ns_joint_floor_mm >>~mm outward as background noise, as targets (<< F.rev_ns_near_f2mm_n_targets >> of the << F.rev_ns_near_n_targets >> near-skull targets), or both. Removing near-skull sources from the background and from the targets have opposite effects, so the exclusion is not conservative by construction.

The dense ratio was << F.rev_ns_near_primary_f2mm_bg_dense_vs_combined_ib_ratio_3dp >> << F.rev_ns_near_primary_f2mm_bg_dense_vs_combined_ib_ci_3dp >> with the near-skull cortex as noise, << F.rev_ns_near_primary_f2mm_targets_dense_vs_combined_ib_ratio_3dp >> << F.rev_ns_near_primary_f2mm_targets_dense_vs_combined_ib_ci_3dp >> with it as targets and << F.rev_ns_near_primary_f2mm_both_dense_vs_combined_ib_ratio_3dp >> << F.rev_ns_near_primary_f2mm_both_dense_vs_combined_ib_ci_3dp >> with both; the site-matched ratio was << F.rev_ns_near_primary_f2mm_bg_matched_vs_combined_ib_ratio_3dp >>, << F.rev_ns_near_primary_f2mm_targets_matched_vs_combined_ib_ratio_3dp >> and << F.rev_ns_near_primary_f2mm_both_matched_vs_combined_ib_ratio_3dp >>, against << F.g2_dense_vs_combined_ib_ratio_3dp >> (dense) and << F.g2_matched_vs_combined_ib_ratio_3dp >> (site-matched) in the primary model. On the near-skull targets themselves, the dense array was ahead by << F.rev_ns_near_primary_f2mm_targets_near_dense_vs_combined_ib_ratio >> << F.rev_ns_near_primary_f2mm_targets_near_dense_vs_combined_ib_ci >>. A refined single-compartment model, whose lead fields converge nearer the skull, repeated the check down to the inner skull with the same result (Fig.~\ref{fig:S5}B).

